sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User / GitOps
    participant API as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant WH as Operator Webhook<br/>Service 443 → 9443/TCP TLS
    participant Op as mcp-lifecycle-operator<br/>(MCPServer controller)
    participant Prov as httproute provider
    participant MCP as MCP server Service<br/>spec.config.port HTTP/HTTPS
    participant GW as Gateway<br/>listener port
    participant Client as External MCP Client
    participant Prom as Prometheus<br/>openshift-monitoring

    Note over User,MCP: Flow 1: Managed MCPServer deployment and verification
    User->>API: Create MCPServer<br/>HTTPS 6443, User token / RBAC
    API->>WH: AdmissionReview / ConversionReview<br/>HTTPS 443→9443, API server admission
    WH-->>API: Allowed / denied (failurePolicy Fail)
    API-->>Op: Watch event (MCPServer)
    Op->>API: Create/Update Deployment, Service, NetworkPolicy<br/>HTTPS 6443, ServiceAccount token
    Op->>MCP: MCP initialize handshake (go-sdk)<br/>HTTP or TLS (CA bundle / system trust / insecureSkipVerify)<br/>No credentials
    MCP-->>Op: serverInfo + capabilities<br/>(401/403 → Verified, AuthSkipped)
    Op->>API: Update status: Verified, address.url, serverInfo<br/>HTTPS 6443, ServiceAccount token

    Note over Op,Client: Flow 2: Gateway exposure (httproute provider)
    Op->>API: Create owned MCPGatewayBinding<br/>HTTPS 6443, SA token
    API-->>Prov: Watch event (MCPGatewayBinding)
    Prov->>API: Read binding ConfigMap + Gateway, create HTTPRoute<br/>HTTPS 6443, SA token
    Prov->>API: Update binding status.url
    Client->>GW: MCP request<br/>HTTP/HTTPS, Gateway-defined TLS/auth
    GW->>MCP: Route via HTTPRoute<br/>spec.config.port
    MCP-->>GW: MCP response
    GW-->>Client: MCP response

    Note over Prom,Op: Flow 3: Metrics scrape
    Prom->>Op: GET /metrics<br/>HTTPS 8443, Bearer token
    Op->>API: TokenReview + SubjectAccessReview
    API-->>Op: Authorized (metrics-reader)
    Op-->>Prom: Prometheus metrics
